From 0b354baf02411e6cec28dbe2cd386b157c444bc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:56:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: scale the page under the bottom tab sheet without a top
 cut

While the bottom-bar tab sheet was up, the page card was scaled from
its top and then clipped by a status-bar-sized inset, and the status
bar was painted with a backdrop colour. That cut the top of the page
and left a straight edge past the card's corner radius.

The page card now scales from the top centre with one rounded outline
on all four corners (radius follows progress) and moves up to the top
of the screen. Ancestor clipping is turned off while the card is up and
restored on close. The status bar stays transparent so the page and its
dim show through it, and the status bar icons switch light or dark from
the luminance of the pixels under them, with hysteresis.

The top-bar sheet and the side drawer do not scale the page.
